From d2f9e0c10d20676619ba9466899dc58a36c9aa75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] RESULT: unparseable-record files are also
 session-bounded

---
 RESULT.md | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/RESULT.md b/RESULT.md
index ed9631f7abdf056aae5d2c19865ed403457d44a4..cbd84576178d9234b1fb995987fe28fe2a898a66 100644
--- a/RESULT.md
+++ b/RESULT.md
@@ -113,7 +113,8 @@ Each head must pass every check below, or it is dropped and counted:
     objects and records).
   * Objects are deleted after processing **and** when their record is dropped (queue full, before the start record,
     or any validation failure).
-  * Files whose record line never arrived (for example, the listener died between writing and printing) remain until
+  * Files whose record line never arrived or could not be parsed (for example, the listener died between writing and
+    printing) remain until
     the session ends, when the whole directory is removed.
   * Session directories marked `OWNER` that a crashed earlier run left behind are removed at start; unmarked
     directories are left alone.
